# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Values prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined into
# the client bundle at build time — this site uses `output: "export"`, so a
# rebuild is required after any change here.

# Web3Forms access key for the contact form.
#
# Get one at https://web3forms.com by registering the inbox that should receive
# enquiries. The key is bound to that address, so it is what decides where
# submissions land — src/lib/content.ts `email` is only used for mailto: links.
#
# This key is public by design (it ships in the client bundle). It is not a
# secret; it lives here so it can differ per environment. Spam protection is the
# honeypot field in src/components/Contact.tsx, plus whatever you enable in the
# Web3Forms dashboard.
#
# .env and .env.local are both gitignored, so deployments do NOT inherit them.
# Set this same variable in the Vercel project settings, or production ships a
# form that cannot deliver.
#
# If unset, the contact form refuses to submit, logs an error to the console,
# and shows the visitor a mailto: fallback.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
